---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EmailSignup from "../components/EmailSignup.astro";
import { DONATION_RAILS } from "../config";
---

<Base title="Transparency" description="Where donations go, who runs the entities that receive them, and where every dollar is accounted for.">
  <span class="pill">The books</span>
  <h1>Transparency</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A donation is a claim on future work. This page is the record of what that claim
    buys, who is legally responsible for spending it, and how those spending decisions
    are checked.
  </p>

  <h2>The entity that receives donations</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      <strong>JustPearlyThings, LLC</strong> — a limited liability company organized under
      U.S. state law, doing business as The Audacity Network. Donations made through this
      site or through <a href="https://theaudacitynetwork.com" rel="noopener">theaudacitynetwork.com</a>
      are processed by Stripe and received by JustPearlyThings, LLC.
    </p>
    <p class="notice" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      <strong>Not tax-deductible.</strong> An LLC is not a 501(c)(3). Contributions here
      are not tax-deductible. If a separate 501(c)(3) is incorporated later — which is
      the intended direction — its EIN, IRS determination letter, and scope will be
      posted on this page in writing, and the donate page will state clearly which
      entity a given contribution routes to.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where the money goes</h2>
  <div class="grid cols-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>1. Content production</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Documentaries, daily show, editors, producers, camera and writing. This is the
        priority allocation and it isn't close — no other line item exists if this one
        stops.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2. Legal defense</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Reporting critically on institutions invites lawsuits, meritorious or not.
        Legal defense is budgeted so the reporting doesn't have to be retracted to
        avoid it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>3. Fieldwork</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Travel and filming — the reporting that requires being physically somewhere,
        with cameras, on someone else's schedule. Receipts are kept and categorized.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>4. Downstream reform (contingent)</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Contributions above the operating cost of the reporting engine flow to
        advocates working on family-court reform — starting with
        <a href="https://www.redonkulas.com" rel="noopener">Terrence Popp</a> and
        <strong>Second Class Citizen</strong>, his 501(c)(3) for combat veterans and
        men inside the family-court system. This is a downstream allocation, activated
        only when the content operation is stable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Where the money does not go</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>Not private benefit outside compensation for work performed on the show.</li>
      <li>
        Not routed through personal accounts. Every donation flows through Stripe,
        Cash App, or Venmo accounts registered to the LLC (or, once incorporated, to
        the 501(c)(3)).
      </li>
      <li>
        Not represented as tax-deductible while the receiving entity is an LLC. When
        that changes, this page changes first.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Who is accountable</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      <strong>Pearl Davis</strong> — founder and operator of JustPearlyThings, LLC.
      Directly responsible for how funds are spent within the LLC.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      When the 501(c)(3) is incorporated, its board of directors will be listed here
      with names, affiliations, and the date each member joined. Pearl has stated
      publicly that Terrence Popp is intended to be on the board.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Annual reports and financials</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">
      The first annual report will be published on this page when the LLC has a
      completed fiscal year of donation-funded operations to report on. Once a
      501(c)(3) is incorporated, its Form 990 will be posted here every year within
      30 days of filing with the IRS, alongside any independently audited financial
      statements.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Until then, per-event fundraising totals and their allocations are posted on the
      <a href="/events">events page</a> for every past event.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Rails and processors</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul class="clean">
      <li><strong>Card donations</strong> — processed by Stripe on The Audacity Network.</li>
      <li><strong>Cash App</strong> — <code>{DONATION_RAILS.cashApp}</code></li>
      <li><strong>Venmo</strong> — <code>{DONATION_RAILS.venmo}</code></li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cryptocurrency</strong> — addresses are being re-verified against an
        official source and will appear on the donate page only after Pearl personally
        confirms them. Sending crypto to an unverified address is irreversible; the
        engineering standard here is 100% or nothing.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>State charity registration</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">
      Charity registration is required by roughly forty U.S. states before soliciting
      donations from their residents as a nonprofit. This obligation applies once the
      501(c)(3) is incorporated. Until then, contributions are solicited only on
      behalf of the LLC, and registration is not required. The state-by-state
      registration list will appear on this page in the same form Beast Philanthropy
      publishes theirs, once the 501(c)(3) is active.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Requesting records</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">
      For a copy of the current financial statement, donation records for a given
      period, or the list of downstream nonprofits that have received grants (once
      applicable), write to
      <a href="mailto:production@theaudacitynetwork.com">production@theaudacitynetwork.com</a>
      with the request in writing. Responses aim to be inside two business weeks.
    </p>
  </div>

  <EmailSignup compact />
</Base>

<style>
  ul.clean { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0; }
  ul.clean li { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
</style>
